Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 01:14:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/20] Don't keep per-torrent piece bitfields for seeds

Each torrent held its piece state up to four times: the cached
torrent_status (pieces and verified_pieces), m_pieces and the have
bitfield of the cached resume data. For a seed they are all ones (or, for
verified_pieces, never read), so keep flags instead and expand them where a
full bitfield is still needed: pieces(), reload() and resume data
preparation. Status updates no longer request verified_pieces.
---
